   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Describing",
     "texto": [
      "After «sein», the adjective **does not change**: **Er ist groß** (he is tall), **Sie ist groß** (she is tall), **Sie sind groß** (they are tall).",
      "In front of a noun it does take an ending; for now, learn these two as fixed phrases: **lange Haare** (long hair) and **kurze Haare** (short hair).",
      "«His» and «her»: **sein** (his) and **ihr** (her). They change like «ein»: **seine Frau** (his wife), **ihr Mann** (her husband)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From 20 to 1,000",
     "texto": [
      "In German, the units are said **before** the tens, joined by **und**: 21 is **einundzwanzig** («one and twenty»), 35 is **fünfunddreißig**. It is all written as one word.",
      "The tens end in **-zig**, except **dreißig** (30). One hundred is **hundert**, two hundred **zweihundert**, and a thousand **tausend**. For 101 you can say **hunderteins**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
